// Call-site arena promotion.
//
// `alloc_and_return` hands fresh storage back to its caller, so on its own the
// classifier would have to call it escaping and let it fall back to the general
// allocator. The caller is the one that knows the answer: `main` prints the value
// and lets the binding die with the frame, so the storage never leaves it.
//
// Every call to the callee bounds the result, so every call passes a real handle
// and the general-allocator arm of the callee's branch never runs. The branch is
// still emitted, because the callee's body does not know which caller reached it
// and one signature has to serve a caller that passes null too. `main` creates the
// arena once, passes it, and releases the whole chunk on the way out.
int* function alloc_and_return() {
    var node = memory.allocate<int>(8);
    node[0] = 42;
    return node;
}

int function main() {
    var n = alloc_and_return();
    print(n[0]);
    return 0;
}
